                <pb facs="0354" n="254" sameAs="frus:frus1884/pg254"/>

                <head>No. 178.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Davis to Mr. West.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1884-08-18"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 18,
                        1884</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to your note of the 25th of
                    June last, in relation to the application of the Government of Canada to land a
                    cable in Washington Territory, I have the honor to inform you that the
                    Department is awaiting further information in regard to the subject before
                    making a full reply thereto.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JOHN DAVIS,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Acting
                        Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
